1. Executive Summary
The product is a Native Android application for advocates combining emergency assistance, verified professional identity, location-aware responder coordination, incident evidence capture, legal information and professional networking. The central experience allows an advocate to raise an SOS, notify selected contacts and eligible nearby verified advocates, share live location when permitted, and track responder progress.
The platform also provides advocate profiles and digital IDs, manual Bar Council enrolment verification, a police/officer directory, SOS history, a moderated professional feed, legal blog/judgment updates and optional premium WhatsApp sharing.
The app must not represent itself as an official emergency service, police dispatch system, guaranteed rescue service or authoritative Bar Council verification source unless separately authorized. Response targets are operational targets, not guarantees.
1.1 Objectives
·       Make SOS activation fast, clear, accessible and auditable.
·       Build trust through transparent manual verification and accurate identity status.
·       Coordinate nearby assistance using consent-based, time-limited location sharing.
·       Maintain incident timelines, responder states and communication records.
·       Support professional networking and curated legal information with moderation and source attribution.
·       Minimise collection and disclosure of sensitive personal, location and incident data.
