5. End-to-End User Journeys
5.1 Onboarding & Verification
1.       User enters mobile number and requests OTP.
2.       Backend sends OTP and applies expiry, cooldown, attempt limits and abuse controls.
3.       User verifies OTP and receives a secure session.
4.       User reviews Terms, Privacy Notice and purpose-specific consents.
5.       User completes profile and submits enrolment details/evidence.
6.       Application enters Pending Review; admin reviews using approved manual checklist.
7.       Admin approves, rejects or requests more information; user receives status and can resubmit/appeal as policy allows.
8.       Approved profile displays platform verification status and digital ID.
5.2 SOS Journey
9.       User opens SOS and sees category, location readiness and data-sharing summary.
10.    User activates SOS using configured hold/countdown interaction; cancellation is available during countdown.
11.    Backend creates one incident using an idempotency key.
12.    Push/SMS orchestration alerts emergency contacts and eligible opted-in verified nearby advocates.
13.    Nearby selection expands through 2 km, 5 km and 10 km according to configured timers and recipient thresholds.
14.    Recipients open incident, review permitted details and accept or decline.
15.    Responder updates Accepted, On the Way and Reached; incident owner sees timestamped status.
16.    Participants use incident group chat or one-to-one entry points; notes/media can be attached.
17.    Owner or authorized operator closes incident; timeline and records are retained under policy.
5.3 Directory and Legal Content
18.    User searches police station/officer directory using location or text filters.
19.    App displays only client-validated records with last-verified date and approved call/map actions.
20.    Editor creates legal update/judgment item with source and court/date metadata.
21.    Editorial and legal reviewer approve content before publication.
22.    Users read, bookmark/share and follow source links; corrections are versioned and logged.
