9. SOS Lifecycle & Business Rules
State
	Meaning
	Allowed next states
	Draft
	SOS screen opened, not activated.
	Countdown, Cancelled
	Countdown
	Activation timer running.
	Active, Cancelled
	Active
	Incident created; alerts/coordination underway.
	Escalated, Resolved, Cancelled
	Escalated
	Higher urgency or wider radius applied.
	Resolved, Cancelled
	Resolved
	Closed by owner/authorized operator.
	Reopened only if policy permits
	Cancelled
	Cancelled before/after activation with reason.
	No ordinary transition
	 
·       Server time is authoritative for event ordering; client time is diagnostic only.
·       Create incident transactionally and use idempotency key to prevent duplicates.
·       Record each expansion stage, radius, recipients count and outcome.
·       Category timers and escalation rules are configurable and auditable.
·       Direct local emergency call action remains available where device permits.
·       App process death must not erase server-side active incident.
·       Closing incident stops location updates and new alerts under approved policy.
