12.2 SOS Android Flow
23.    User action creates a local activation request with unique idempotency key.
24.    ViewModel controls countdown/cancel state and prevents duplicate action.
25.    Repository calls SOS API; backend persists incident and outbox event transactionally.
26.    Notification workers dispatch recipient alerts; FCM/deep link refreshes incident state.
27.    Location foreground service starts only with valid permission, visible notification and policy justification.
28.    Location updates upload with accuracy and timestamp; encrypted queue is used only if approved.
29.    On relaunch, app fetches active incident from backend and reconciles pending work.
12.3 Offline & Process Resilience
·       Persist minimum SOS draft data encrypted and with bounded retention.
·       WorkManager is for retryable work, not a guarantee of immediate emergency delivery.
·       Do not show server-confirmed active SOS until server confirms.
·       Explain offline, GPS-disabled, permission-denied and SMS-handoff states.
·       Avoid continuous location tracking outside active, disclosed use.
