14. Security, Privacy & Compliance
14.1 Security Controls
·       TLS 1.2+ for all traffic; secure authentication, short-lived access tokens, refresh rotation and revocation.
·       Server-side RBAC and object-level authorization for profiles, incidents, media and admin actions.
·       Encryption at rest for database, backups, object storage and sensitive fields.
·       Android Keystore for device secrets; no private API keys embedded in APK.
·       OTP abuse controls, rate limiting, fraud detection and secure account recovery.
·       Audit admin access, verification decisions, incident access, exports, media access and role changes.
·       SAST/DAST, dependency scanning, penetration testing, release signing and secure CI/CD.
·       Redact tokens, phone numbers, enrolment data, coordinates and message content from logs.
14.2 Privacy Requirements
·       Identify data controller/processor roles and publish clear privacy notice.
·       Collect only data needed for declared purposes; separate optional profile/community data.
·       Location sharing is incident-scoped, visible and time-limited; no always-on tracking by default.
·       Define retention/deletion for identity evidence, location, media, messages and content.
·       Provide grievance/contact route and access/correction/deletion processes as applicable.
·       Conduct privacy impact assessment for location, emergency contacts, media and identity verification.
·       Obtain Indian legal review for applicable data protection, telecom, intermediary, copyright and Play policies; this PRD is not legal advice.
14.3 Safety & Abuse Prevention
·       Countdown/cancel and rate limits reduce accidental/malicious SOS without obstructing genuine emergencies.
·       Provide report/block tools and responder misconduct reporting.
·       Limit exact location to need-to-know roles and time-bound access.
·       Do not expose sensitive incident details in public feed or lock-screen previews.
·       Define human review and appeal for false SOS abuse or account restrictions.
